 (267,332,'Division depth changes the apparent value of a lower seed','The commentator interprets invitation/decline outcomes and compares the resulting alliances’ scoring depth, including partially completed autonomous algae work.','Do not identify seed order with an ordinal ranking of every robot’s ability. A lower-seed captain may obtain a coherent three-robot package. Actual reasons for declining require a team account; the video supplies an outside interpretation.'),
 (802,867,'Practice can compensate for difficult L1 presentation','The source praises placing and arranging L1 coral even when the mechanism presents it less conveniently than a flat horizontal release.','The available packing pattern and placement speed depend on geometry and driver practice together. A skilled workaround is not proof that the geometry has no cost, nor that a copied robot will perform it immediately.'),
 (1337,1402,'Containment changes which remaining partners decide the match','The Curie account describes 1771 committing substantial time to containing 3005 after an algae incursion, leaving the other robots to determine the scoring race.','A captain can rationally sacrifice its own output if the denied opponent is more important and the remaining partners have the advantage. Those comparisons need role-specific capability and autonomous context, not simply adding season-final EPA.')
