 (196,261,'A large funnel changes station approach tolerance','The narrator describes rapid station contact/centering and 2767 combining available algae with defense; he also notes prepared multiple coral at a station as an anti-defense option.','The funnel’s value includes permissible driver error and minimized settle time. The prepared supply and human-player coordination belong to the cycle system. A fast wall approach must still be tested for damage, bounce and safe legal delivery.'),
 (589,654,'Auto misses can dominate a later tactical comparison','The source compares a revised matchup with an altered autonomous gap, including missed coral/algae, while acknowledging that even algae theft alone may not reverse the margin.','Avoid attributing the entire result to the most novel tactic. Preserve missed auto, breakage and substitutions as competing explanations. Resource parity can reflect both alliances actively stealing rather than an absence of strategic importance.'),
